# Why does this file exist? The host image's build context is an allowlist: only what its Dockerfile copies is sent
# to the builder, so no secret, build output (crimson_noir_os/target is gigabytes) or test file can reach it; the
# closure stage then picks the host's own files out of src/, and the page's components, shaders and styles are kept
# out here too.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!LICENSE
!NOTICE.md
!src/
src/**/*.test.ts
src/**/*.tsx
src/**/*.wgsl
src/**/*.css
src/**/*.d.ts
!tools/net/closure.mjs
!tools/net/mint-token.mjs
!tools/net/image-check.mjs
!crimson_noir_os/containment.lock
!crimson_noir_os/containment.seal
